# Project Helios

<!-- sec:sec_charter -->
## Charter

The program exists to find a thermostable lead from the NW-200 scaffold series for oral delivery.{{artifact:8f6f9e00-7e50-4199-8443-dc7977d167d6-document-block-1}} It is headed by [[Dana Whitfield]].{{artifact:8f6f9e00-7e50-4199-8443-dc7977d167d6-document-block-2}}

<!-- sec:sec_budget -->
## Budget

Fiscal 2024 funding is USD 2.4 million, reviewed each quarter by the portfolio committee.{{artifact:8f6f9e00-7e50-4199-8443-dc7977d167d6-document-block-3}}

<!-- sec:sec_success_criterion -->
## Success criterion

A lead must keep at least 80 percent of its activity after two weeks at 40 degrees Celsius.{{artifact:8f6f9e00-7e50-4199-8443-dc7977d167d6-document-block-4}}

<!-- sec:sec_lead_decision -->
## Lead decision  [2024-09-09]

The portfolio committee approved NW-217 as the lead on 9 September 2024.{{artifact:bb4de0e9-1f4e-4c2e-88aa-efcd4352de0c-document-block-1}}
